def LAD(a,b,c,d,e,f,g): return [a,b,c,d,e,f,g]
COURSES = [
dict(slug='automobile', title='Automobile and Electric Vehicle Servicing', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Learn how a modern vehicle works, how to inspect and service it safely, and how to run a small workshop that keeps records and customers.',
 outs=[('Define','the main systems of a petrol, diesel and electric vehicle.'),('Apply','a safe inspection and service routine with a written job card.'),('Analyse','faults using symptoms, readings and a fault tree.'),('Evaluate','repair-or-replace choices on cost, safety and life left.'),('Create','a workshop plan with bays, tools, records and customer follow-up.')],
 task='Inspect, diagnose and service a light vehicle, and record the work so another technician can repeat it.',
 cond='About 10 weeks part-time. A workshop bay or training vehicle, basic hand tools, a scan tool, a multimeter, a mentor on site.',
 standard='Every job follows the written safety steps, readings are logged with units, the fault is found before parts are changed, and the customer receives a clear job card.',
 who='School leavers, ITI and diploma students, mechanics moving to electric vehicles, small workshop owners.', req='None; basic reading and arithmetic.',
 mods=[
 M('Shop safety and vehicle systems','Define',4,['Name the main systems: engine or motor, transmission, brakes, steering, suspension, cooling, electrical, body.','Wear and check protective gear; keep fire, fuel and fluid spill rules in view.','Lift a vehicle only at the marked points and with rated stands.','High-voltage packs need isolation steps and trained people; never touch orange cables without the written procedure.'],'A car on a two-post lift: lift pads set under the marked points, wheels chocked, a stand placed, then the lift lowered onto the stand before work starts.','Draw a labelled sketch of one vehicle with all eight systems and write the five safety rules for your bay.','Sketch names all systems correctly; five rules cover lifting, fire, fluids, electrical and gear.','Where do you place lift pads?','At the vehicle maker marked lifting points.'),
 M('Engine and motor basics','Explain',5,['Four strokes: intake, compression, power, exhaust; diesel ignites by compression, petrol by spark.','Electric motor: stored battery energy turns the rotor; the controller sets speed and torque.','Hybrid: both systems share the drive; software chooses the mix.','Warning lights and sounds are first clues, not the answer.'],'A car that shakes at idle: the technician notes misfire code on cylinder 2 and swaps coil positions to see if the fault moves.','Explain in 150 words how petrol, diesel and electric drive differ, using a diagram.','Explanation is correct, uses the four strokes, and names one advantage and one limit of each.','What starts combustion in a diesel engine?','Heat from compressing the air.'),
 M('Inspection and routine service','Apply',5,['Follow the maker service schedule: oil and filter, air filter, coolant, brake fluid, tyre pressure and tread.','Torque bolts to the written value with a torque wrench; mark them once tight.','Write each check as done, adjusted, replaced or advised.','Return old parts to the customer if asked; dispose of oil and batteries by the local rule.'],'A routine service job card: engine oil 3.5 L replaced, tyre pressures set to 2.2 bar, brake pad 4 mm advised for next visit.','Complete a job card for a full service on a training vehicle.','Every line shows a reading or a clear action and the card is signed with date and odometer.','What are the four ways to mark a checked item?','Done, adjusted, replaced, advised.'),
 M('Brakes, steering and suspension','Apply',5,['Measure disc thickness and pad depth against minimum values.','Bleed brakes in the maker order and test the pedal before the road test.','Check play in steering joints and bushes; look for leaks on dampers.','Alignment is measured, not guessed.'],'Pad thickness 2.5 mm against a 3 mm minimum: replace both pads on the axle, measure the disc, and test-drive at low speed.','Carry out a brake inspection and write the pass or fail with numbers.','Readings are in millimetres with the limit beside them; the test drive is recorded.','Why replace pads in axle pairs?','To keep braking balanced on both wheels.'),
 M('Electrical and diagnostics','Analyse',5,['Use a multimeter for voltage, resistance and continuity; learn safe ranges.','Read fault codes and live data; codes point to a circuit, not always a part.','Fault tree: symptom, likely causes, cheapest test first, confirm before replacing.','Battery health: voltage rest, load test and charging rate.'],'No-start with a clicking relay: battery rests at 11.6 V, load test fails, charging system is fine; replace the battery, not the starter.','Diagnose a seeded fault using a fault tree and write the proof.','The fault is confirmed with a measurement before parts are changed.','What comes before replacing a part?','A test that confirms the fault.'),
 M('Electric vehicle systems','Analyse',5,['Battery pack, cells, battery management system, charger, inverter, motor, thermal loop.','Charging types: slow home charging, fast public charging; know connectors in use locally.','Range depends on speed, load, temperature and driving style.','Only trained people open high-voltage parts; others read data and do visible checks.'],'A customer says range dropped 20%: the data shows high tyre drag from low pressure and a cold morning; pressure is set and a driving tip given.','Explain to a customer, in plain words, why range changes, with three causes.','Three causes are right and the explanation avoids jargon.','Who may open a high-voltage battery pack?','Only people trained and authorised with the written procedure.'),
 M('Workshop operations and records','Evaluate',5,['Bay plan, tool list, calibration dates and spare stock.','Quote before work, approve extra work in writing, invoice on time.','Track repeat visits and comebacks as a quality measure.','Customer follow-up after three days and thirty days.'],'A small workshop logs 120 jobs in a month, 4 comebacks; the owner finds two came from one rushed technician and adds a second check.','Build a one-page workshop plan with bay layout, records and two quality measures.','Plan shows layout, record forms, and two measures with a monthly target.','Name one quality measure for a workshop.','Comebacks per 100 jobs.'),
 M('Capstone: inspect, diagnose, report','Create',4,['Choose a training vehicle and a scenario.','Inspect, diagnose, repair or advise, and write the report.','Present the report to a mentor and a mock customer.','Reflect: what would you do differently?'],'A final report: three findings, two repairs done, one advised, total time 3.5 h, customer questions answered.','Run the full job and present it in five minutes.','Job card, readings, proof of fault and customer summary are all present and correct.','What does a good final report contain?','Findings, actions, readings, advice and a customer summary.')],
 extra=[('Name the first step before any lift.','Check the lift points and wheel chocks.'),('Why log units next to readings?','So anyone can repeat or check the reading.')],
 rubric=[('Safety','Steps skipped','Written steps followed','Steps followed and corrected for others'),('Diagnosis','Parts changed by guess','Fault proved before repair','Fault tree used and shared'),('Records','Missing details','Complete job card','Complete card plus trend notes'),('Customer','Jargon only','Clear summary','Summary plus follow-up booked')],
 ladder=LAD('Know the parts and the safety rules.','Describe how engine, brakes and electric drive work.','Do routine checks under supervision.','Service and diagnose common faults alone.','Handle electric and hybrid diagnosis and complex faults.','Lead a workshop, train others, set quality measures.','Design workshop systems, standards and training for a region.'),
 jobs=['Vehicle service technician','Electric vehicle technician','Workshop supervisor','Service adviser','Small workshop owner']),

dict(slug='electronics', title='Electronics Assembly and Testing', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Build and test electronic circuits and boards, read schematics, solder safely, and report faults with measured proof.',
 outs=[('Define','voltage, current, resistance and power with units.'),('Apply','safe soldering and assembly to a written standard.'),('Analyse','a circuit with a multimeter and an oscilloscope.'),('Evaluate','a board for fit to its specification.'),('Create','a small tested product and its build record.')],
 task='Assemble a small electronic board from a schematic, test it against its specification and record the results.',
 cond='About 8 weeks part-time. Bench with soldering station, multimeter, power supply, component kit, safety glasses.',
 standard='Joints are clean and sound, readings sit inside the stated limits, and every step is recorded so another person can rebuild the board.',
 who='Diploma and degree students, hobbyists, repair technicians, small manufacturers.', req='Basic arithmetic.',
 mods=[
 M('Bench safety and electricity basics','Define',4,['Voltage is push, current is flow, resistance is opposition; Ohm law links them.','Power equals voltage times current; know the heat it makes.','Static damage: wrist strap, mat and bags protect chips.','Hot iron, fumes and small parts: ventilate, rest the iron in its stand.'],'A 5 V supply across a 250 ohm resistor gives 20 mA and 0.1 W; a quarter-watt resistor is safe.','Solve five Ohm law problems and write six bench rules.','All answers include units and are correct; rules cover heat, fumes, static, eyes, power and tidiness.','What does Ohm law link?','Voltage, current and resistance.'),
 M('Components and schematics','Explain',5,['Resistors, capacitors, diodes, LEDs, transistors, chips: what each does.','Read symbols, reference marks and values; colour codes and markings.','Polarity: diodes, electrolytic capacitors and chips have a right way round.','A bill of materials lists every part with its quantity.'],'A schematic shows R1 at 330 ohm in series with an LED; the bill of materials lists one resistor and one LED for the stage.','Annotate a given schematic and make its bill of materials.','Every part is named, valued and counted; polarity marked.','Which parts need correct polarity?','Diodes, LEDs, electrolytic capacitors and chips.'),
 M('Soldering and assembly','Apply',6,['Tin the tip, heat the pad and lead together, feed solder, remove solder then iron.','A good joint is shiny and shaped like a small cone.','Fit low parts first, then taller ones; trim leads after soldering.','Inspect with a magnifier for bridges and cold joints.'],'A cold joint looks dull and ball-shaped; the technician reheats it with a little fresh solder until it flows.','Assemble a kit board with at least 30 joints.','No bridges, no cold joints on inspection, and all parts correct.','What does a good joint look like?','Shiny and cone-shaped.'),
 M('Measurement and testing','Apply',6,['Use a multimeter for voltage, resistance and continuity.','Power up slowly with a current limit and watch for heat.','Check test points against expected values in the spec.','Use an oscilloscope for signals: set scale, trigger and read the period.'],'A 1 kHz square wave shows 1 ms per cycle on the scope; the technician sets 0.5 ms per division and counts two divisions.','Test your board at five points and record expected and measured values.','All readings are inside limits or the difference is explained.','Why power up with a current limit?','To avoid damage if there is a short.'),
 M('Fault finding','Analyse',6,['Start with visual checks, then power, then signal path.','Split the circuit in halves to find which half fails.','Compare to a working board.','Write the root cause, not only the fix.'],'Board dead: supply reads 0 V at the regulator output; the input is fine, so the regulator or its load fails; a short on the load is found.','Find a seeded fault and write the root cause.','Root cause is proved with a reading and the fix is checked.','What is the first fault-finding step?','Look carefully, then check power.'),
 M('Quality, standards and records','Evaluate',5,['Work to a workmanship standard with clear accept and reject examples.','Record batch, date, test results and who built it.','Rework policy: fix once, then scrap or escalate.','Safe handling and disposal of electronic waste.'],'A batch of 40 boards: 38 pass first time, 2 reworked; yield is 95% first pass.','Build a one-page record sheet and use it on five boards.','Sheet is complete for all five boards and the yield is calculated.','How is first-pass yield found?','Boards passing first time divided by boards built.'),
 M('Small product design','Create',5,['Choose a simple need such as a night light or a water alarm.','Draw the schematic, choose parts, estimate cost.','Build a prototype and test.','Write a short user note.'],'A water-level alarm using a transistor and buzzer; cost estimate 140 rupees; tested at three levels.','Design, build and test a small product.','Prototype works to spec, cost is stated, and the user note is clear.','What goes in a user note?','What it does, how to use it safely, and how to reset it.'),
 M('Capstone: build and report','Create',4,['Take a given schematic and build to the end.','Test and fix any faults.','Write a build record and a one-page summary.','Present to peers.'],'A final board with a record showing 3 tests, 1 fault fixed, and 2 hours total.','Build, test and present.','Board meets spec, record is complete, and the talk is clear.','What proves a board meets its spec?','Test readings inside the stated limits.')],
 extra=[('Name two static protection items.','Wrist strap and anti-static mat.'),('Why keep a bill of materials?','To buy and check the right parts every time.')],
 rubric=[('Soldering','Bridges and cold joints','Sound joints','Sound joints and coaching others'),('Testing','Guessing','Readings recorded','Readings with limits and trend'),('Fault finding','Random swaps','Method followed','Root cause shared'),('Records','Gaps','Complete','Complete with yield')],
 ladder=LAD('Name basic components and bench rules.','Explain what circuits do.','Solder and test a kit under supervision.','Build, test and fix boards alone.','Design boards, set test plans and handle high-volume work.','Lead production quality and train others.','Set product standards and supply plans across sites.'),
 jobs=['Electronics technician','Test technician','Repair technician','Production operator','Small-device maker']),

dict(slug='information-technologies', title='Information Technology Support and Practice', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Support computers, networks and basic software for a small organisation, keep data safe and solve user problems with records.',
 outs=[('Define','the parts of a computer, a network and an operating system.'),('Apply','set-up, update and backup tasks with a checklist.'),('Analyse','a user problem from symptoms to cause.'),('Evaluate','the risk of a setting or a habit.'),('Create','a support plan with a help log and a backup test.')],
 task='Set up and look after ten computers and a small network for a small office, and fix user problems with a logged ticket.',
 cond='About 10 weeks part-time. Two or more computers or virtual machines, a router, internet access, a mentor.',
 standard='Systems are updated, backups restore in a test, passwords follow the policy, and each ticket has symptom, cause, fix and time.',
 who='Students, career changers, office staff, small-business owners.', req='Basic computer use.',
 mods=[
 M('Computer and operating system basics','Define',4,['Processor, memory, storage, display, input and ports.','The operating system manages files, apps and users.','Accounts: standard users for daily work, an administrator for changes.','Updates fix security holes; schedule them.'],'A laptop running slow: storage is 98% full; clearing 30 GB and disabling 6 start-up apps brings boot time from 4 minutes to 1.','List the parts of your computer with sizes and write a monthly update routine.','List matches the real machine and the routine names day, task and owner.','Why use a standard account daily?','It limits damage from mistakes and malware.'),
 M('Networks and internet','Explain',5,['Router, switch, wireless access point, cables, IP address, DNS.','Home and office networks: separate guest wifi from staff.','Test with ping and a speed test; record the result.','Share files and printers with permissions.'],'A printer that disappears: its address changed; assign a fixed address in the router and the problem ends.','Draw a network diagram for a ten-person office and list the settings.','Diagram shows all devices and the guest and staff split.','What does DNS do?','Turns names into addresses.'),
 M('Security and backups','Apply',5,['Passwords: long phrases, a password manager and a second step.','Spot phishing: sender, link, urgency, attachment.','Backups: three copies, two media, one away; test a restore.','Protect personal data under the local law.'],'A restore test: the finance folder of 2 GB is restored in 12 minutes to a spare machine, files open correctly.','Set up a backup and prove a restore.','Restore is done, timed and recorded; two files opened.','What is the 3-2-1 rule?','Three copies, two media types, one copy away.'),
 M('Setting up and maintaining machines','Apply',5,['Clean install or image, drivers, standard software list.','Disk encryption on laptops.','Asset list: serial, user, date, warranty.','Retire machines by wiping data and recycling.'],'Ten laptops are imaged in one afternoon with a standard list and encryption on; the asset sheet lists each serial.','Prepare two machines and update the asset sheet.','Machines match the list; encryption is on; sheet is complete.','Why keep an asset list?','To track, support and retire machines properly.'),
 M('Help desk method','Analyse',6,['Ticket fields: who, what, when, impact, steps, fix, time.','Ask open questions and repeat the problem back.','Try the cheapest, safest fix first.','Record the cause so the same problem is faster next time.'],'A ticket: cannot send email; cause is a full mailbox; fix is archive older mail; time 12 minutes.','Handle five practice tickets and log them.','Every ticket has cause, fix and time and the user confirms it works.','What fields belong on a ticket?','Who, what, when, impact, steps, fix and time.'),
 M('Office software and data','Apply',5,['Documents, sheets and email: templates and shared folders.','Naming rules for files and version control.','Simple formulas and charts for a report.','Basic database ideas: tables, records, search.'],'A shared sheet with a monthly sales table; a total formula and a chart show a dip in week 3.','Build a shared folder structure and a sheet with a chart.','Names follow the rule; formulas are right; chart is labelled.','Why use file naming rules?','To find and compare files quickly.'),
 M('Cloud and remote work','Evaluate',5,['Cloud storage and software as a service: benefits and risks.','Video meetings and remote access with safe settings.','Cost: per user, per month; compare options.','Data location and legal rules.'],'Two cloud options compared: option A is cheaper per user but stores data abroad, which fails the data rule; option B is chosen.','Compare two cloud options in a table with a recommendation.','Table has cost, security, data rule and a reason.','What is a risk of cloud storage?','Loss of control over where data sits and who can reach it.'),
 M('Capstone: support plan for a small office','Create',4,['Gather needs from a mock office.','Plan machines, network, backups, security and help desk.','Run a restore test and one mock incident.','Present the plan and results.'],'A plan for 10 users with a monthly cost, a restore test passed in 15 minutes and one phishing incident handled.','Write and present the plan.','Plan covers all areas, test results are shown and risks are ranked.','What must a support plan prove?','That backups restore and problems get logged and fixed.')],
 extra=[('What makes a good password?','Long, unique, and kept in a manager with a second step.'),('Why test a restore?','A backup is only useful if it restores.')],
 rubric=[('Security','Weak passwords','Policy followed','Policy plus training for users'),('Backups','Never tested','Restore proved','Restore timed and scheduled'),('Tickets','Missing details','Complete','Complete with causes grouped'),('Planning','Ad hoc','Documented','Costed and risk-ranked')],
 ladder=LAD('Name the parts of a computer and a network.','Describe safe habits and common threats.','Do basic set-up and support under supervision.','Support a small office alone.','Design networks, security and cloud use for several sites.','Lead an IT team and audit controls.','Set IT standards and strategy for an organisation.'),
 jobs=['IT support technician','Help desk agent','Junior system administrator','Office IT coordinator','Small-business IT adviser']),
]
